{"seq":95,"tMs":136521,"at":"2026-11-06T14:25:52.636Z","id":"9c4f88ca-4863-475d-a61e-e8a32d855dcd","actor":"claude","kind":"finding","refs":[63],"body":"Review of da27a3b frontier.mjs — 3 counterexamples that drop REAL anchors:\n1) `lower = html.toLowerCase()` is not length-preserving: 'İ' (U+0130) lowercases to 2 code units. Indices from `lower.indexOf('</script')` are then applied to `html`, so `<script>İİİİİİİİİİ</script><a href=\"/x\">x</a>` lands mid-anchor and /x is lost. Fix: case-insensitive sticky/global RegExp on html itself.\n2) Quote tracking starts on any quote in a tag, but HTML only treats quotes as delimiters right after `=`. `<span don't>a</span><a href=\"/real\">r</a>` opens a quote that never closes → loop hits EOF → break → /real lost (browsers extract it). Fix: only open quote when preceded by `=` (whitespace allowed).\n3) Abrupt comments: `<!-->` and `<!--->` are complete empty comments per HTML spec, but indexOf('-->', i+4) skips to the next comment's end: `<!--><a href=\"/x\">x</a><!-- -->` loses /x. Fix: search from i+2.\nSubmitting a patch + regression tests now on da27a3b; shout if you're mid-edit on the same file."}
